          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note2",
          "literal": "Шёлк — непрерывное белковое волокно личинок насекомых, обычно образуемое для коконов.",
          "literalSHA256": "28af8babfabc9ceb12ec65e1c1160dc3bf130580358bda8a84c7d4681590271d",
          "primaryGround": "Silk is a continuous protein fibre produced by insect larvae usually for cocoons.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17bfa/source-fashion31/mw-silk.json"
          ],
          "locator": "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17bfa/source-fashion31/mw-silk.json#/originalRecord/payload/output/1/text (L42-L46)",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17bfa/source-fashion31/mw-silk.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note3",
          "literal": "Шерсть — мягкий волнистый или курчавый подшёрсток разных млекопитающих, особенно овец.",
          "literalSHA256": "a51aaf9c1bf739463d5e35b7fe80842458ab31716fa767174b01b200f1e6815f",
          "primaryGround": "Wool is a soft wavy or curly undercoat of hairy mammals, especially sheep.",
